const projects=[
{slug:'almaymaar',name:'Almaymaar',line:'I changed how a company thinks about its brand.',summary:'Replaced reactive posting with a named content system — corporate positioning end to end.',image:'/assets/almaymaar-1.png',blocks:[['Changing the story real estate tells.','Pakistani real estate had become predictable. Developers talked about projects, prices, amenities and promises. Every brand sounded like it was selling the same dream. Almaymaar needed a different belief system. So we stopped treating content as a stream of promotional posts and built an editorial system around why this way, from the site, and people & places.'],['Why This Way','We challenged the way Pakistani developers sell. Instead of asking people to believe another property promise, we built a point of view around why Almaymaar builds the way it does. Architecture. Decisions. Materials. Intent. The thinking behind the development became part of the brand.\n\nThe objective wasn’t to sell harder. It was to build belief.'],['From the Site','Construction stopped being something to hide until the finished product. We took people onto the site, showed the progress, the materials, the decisions and the people behind the build. The promise became visible.'],['People & Places','Beyond the buildings, we explored the people, places, culture and details surrounding them. The brand became a place you could experience before you bought into it.'],['The result','8,000+ organic followers in 10 months. An audience built around a real-estate brand without turning the feed into a property catalogue.']],gallery:['/assets/almaymaar-2.png','/assets/almaymaar-3.png']},
{slug:'harsukh',name:'The Harsukh',line:'I built belief, and it moved the inventory.',summary:'Helped take a flagship from 15 to 68 units sold in one year.',image:'/assets/harsukh-1.jpeg',blocks:[['A place without an identity','Harsukh was a beautiful place without much of an identity around it, so I wanted to build the brand around the people and the reality behind making it.'],['Show what nobody else was showing','Instead of hiding the construction, we took people to the site, introduced the labourers and showed the progress, something rarely seen in Pakistani real estate. We told the story of what it actually takes to build in the extreme weather of Galiyat.'],['Then we built the world around it','I shaped the interiors, developed AI-led visual storytelling for the campaign, built presenter-led lead-generation content and helped give Harsukh a visual and narrative language of its own.'],['And it moved','The brand grew to 7,000 organic followers in a single month, while the flagship had sold 15 units when I joined and 68 during my first year. The story, the place and the business finally started moving together.']],gallery:['/assets/harsukh-2.jpeg']},
{slug:'downtownlahore',name:'Downtown Lahore',line:'I sell a place by selling the idea of it.',summary:'A TVC made to turn a destination into a national conversation.',blocks:[['The idea of a destination','Downtown Lahore needed to feel larger than a development. The work framed it as a destination with its own energy, rhythm and cultural pull.'],['A national conversation','The campaign used film and a clear central thought to make the place memorable before audiences ever arrived. The goal was to sell the feeling of being there, not simply list what would be built.'],['My role','Creative direction, narrative development and campaign storytelling.']]},
{slug:'crafeupstairs',name:'Crafé Upstairs',line:'I turned a space into a story people bought.',summary:'A reveal that turned a hidden coffee space into something people wanted to discover.',blocks:[['A space that needed a reason to gather','Crafé was already a coffee space in Cantt, Lahore, but its upstairs area was largely undiscovered. The challenge was to introduce it without making the launch feel like another restaurant announcement.'],['We started with the thought behind Crafé','I created a storytelling film around the founding thought of Crafé, using that idea as the starting point for the reveal. I also developed the supporting content and launch material around the same narrative.'],['Then we let people discover it','The film became the centrepiece of the reveal. The result was simple: people showed up, the upstairs became a place to gather, and the tables filled.']]},
{slug:'kiapakistan',name:'KIA Pakistan',line:"I wrote a ‘movement’ that inspired.",summary:'A launch film built around two teams, two SUVs, and a race where nobody could lose.',blocks:[['A race where nobody could lose','KIA was launching the all-new Sorento and Sportage. Put two cars in a race and someone has to lose. We needed the excitement of a real competition without making either SUV feel like the losing product.'],['So we made the difference the story','I wrote the concept around two teams, six creators and two SUVs racing from Islamabad towards Nathiagali. The Sportage brought energy and agility, while the Sorento took a more effortless approach. The cars experienced their features through the creators and the way each team chose to travel.'],['And then Junejo stopped the race','Midway through the journey, Irfan Junejo spotted the perfect golden-hour light. The team wanted to keep moving, but he stopped anyway. “Race ruk sakti hai... golden hour aur content paglu nahi.” The Sorento arrived first by only a few seconds. Nobody really lost.'],['My role','Ad concept, narrative structure and dialogue. The concept was handed to the agency for production and execution.']]},
{slug:'imarat',name:'IMARAT',line:'I turn a dry mechanic into a story.',summary:'Making large, complicated places understandable and worth caring about.',blocks:[['I learned to make big places understandable','IMARAT was where I began working at the intersection of real estate, marketing and storytelling. Projects like Grand Bazaar and Mall of IMARAT were enormous ideas that needed to be understood quickly by people who might eventually invest in them.'],['We turned the project into a story','For Grand Bazaar, I worked on the concept and messaging and presented the film myself. For Mall of IMARAT, I developed explainer content around its location, architectural scale and commercial proposition. The videos became sales tools as much as marketing pieces.'],['My role','Creative & Brand Manager — concept and messaging, brand storytelling, project marketing, on-camera presentation and investor communication.'],['This is the beginning of the story','Before I was building brand systems, I was learning how to take something massive, complicated and commercial and find the story inside it.']]},
{slug:'chakor',name:'Chakor Ventures',line:'I found my craft in the making of a city.',summary:'Stories built around places made to change the skyline.',blocks:[["I made the brand’s promise visible",'Chakor Ventures had a simple idea at the heart of its brand: achieving heights. I wanted to turn that line from something a brand says into something the audience could actually see.'],['So I climbed to the top of it','For Citadel 7, I developed a short-form reel around one simple hook: get on the crane. I climbed high above the construction site and delivered the brand story from a perspective people would not normally see. The crane became the idea.'],['Then I made the complicated stuff watchable','For the 60–40 campaign, I created a conversational format where I appeared as both interviewer and guest, unpacking the payment structure as content rather than a sales pitch.'],['My role','Creative Strategist — creative concept, campaign ideas, brand messaging, content strategy, on-camera presentation and digital campaigns.']]}
];
const app=document.querySelector('#app');
const esc=s=>s.replace(/[&<>"']/g,m=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#039;'}[m]));
function home(){return `<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="intro">Hi, I’m Wasib Imdad</span><h1 class="display">Creative<em>Maker</em>Storyteller</h1><div class="hero-bottom"><span class="eyebrow">What I do</span><div><p>I find the story in an idea, then build the world around it. Across brands, campaigns, places and films, I turn what needs to be said into something people can see, feel, and remember.</p><a class="cta" href="/work/" data-link>View work</a></div></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="/assets/hero.png" alt="Wasib Imdad seated in a studio portrait"><span class="media-label">Creative Director · Lahore</span></div></section><section class="statement"><span class="eyebrow">I create</span><h2>Brands. Places.<br><em>Stories.</em></h2></section><a class="film" href="/work/" data-link aria-label="Explore Wasib’s selected work"><img src="/assets/polaroids.png" alt="A selection of Wasib’s creative work"><span class="play">View</span></a>`}
function work(){const rows=[
['almaymaar','I changed how a company thinks about its brand','Replaced reactive posting with a named content system — corporate positioning end to end.'],
['harsukh','I built belief & it moved the inventory.','Helped take a flagship from a mere 14 to 65 units sold – in a year!'],
['downtownlahore','I sell a place by selling the idea of it.','A TVC made to turn a destination into a national conversation.'],
['crafeupstairs','I turned a space into a story people bought.','A reveal that turned a hidden coffee space into something people wanted to discover.'],
['kiapakistan',"I wrote a 'Movement' that inspired.",'A launch film for KIA Pakistan – a race between the Sorento and Sportage.'],
['chakor','I turn a dry mechanic into a story.','Invented a format to make a payment structure something people could actually grasp.'],
['imarat','I found my craft in the making of a city.','Stories built around places made to change the skyline.']
];return `<section class="portfolio-panel"><header class="portfolio-intro"><h1>Portfolio</h1><p>A selection of work spanning products, brands, content and creative direction.</p></header><div class="portfolio-rows">${rows.map(r=>`<a class="portfolio-row" href="/${r[0]}/" data-link><h2>${r[1]}</h2><p>${r[2]}</p><span class="portfolio-meta"><span>${({almaymaar:"ALMAYMAAR",harsukh:"The Harsukh",downtownlahore:"Vision Group, Samaa TV",crafeupstairs:"Crafe Lahore",kiapakistan:"KIA Pakistan",chakor:"Chakor Ventures",imarat:"IMARAT"})[r[0]]}</span><span>${({almaymaar:"2026",harsukh:"2026",downtownlahore:"2025",crafeupstairs:"2025",kiapakistan:"2025",chakor:"2024",imarat:"2020–2023"})[r[0]]}</span></span></a>`).join('')}</div></section>`}
function almaymaarCaseStudy(){return `<section class="almaymaar-hero"><div class="almaymaar-opening"><img class="almaymaar-opening-image" src="/assets/almaymaar-hero.png" alt="A mirrored crystal rising from broken rock" width="1665" height="944" fetchpriority="high"><div class="almaymaar-opening-caption"><span class="case-kicker">Almaymaar · Selected work</span><p>Head of Marketing (Brand Strategy, Creative Direction, Content Strategy, Corporate Positioning)</p></div></div><div class="almaymaar-title"><h1>I changed how a company thinks about its brand.</h1><p>Replaced reactive posting with a named content system — corporate positioning end to end.</p></div><a class="almaymaar-reel" href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DcAjfpxoj35/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-full-grid.jpg" alt="Almaymaar editorial content system"><span class="reel-play">Watch the flagship reel ↗</span></a></section>
<article class="almaymaar-case">
  <section class="almaymaar-intro"><p>Almaymaar is a Pakistani real-estate developer with more than 13 million sq. ft. under construction across Karachi, Lahore, Islamabad, Attock and Galiyat.</p><h2>I stopped asking,<br>“What should we post?”</h2><p class="answer">And started asking: <em>What does a real-estate company actually have to say?</em></p></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-before"><div class="almaymaar-section-head"><span>Before</span><h2>Lots of content.<br>Very little reason to remember who said it.</h2></div><div class="before-pair"><figure><img src="/assets/almaymaar-before-1.jpg" alt="Almaymaar social feed before the new content system"></figure><figure><img src="/assets/almaymaar-before-2.jpg" alt="Almaymaar social feed before Wasib joined"></figure></div><p class="almaymaar-caption">Almaymaar, before I joined.</p></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The problem</span><div><p>Real-estate content seemed to live at two extremes. It was either selling something — book now, invest today, limited inventory, highest ROI — or trying so hard not to sell that it became surface-level information.</p><p>Looking at Almaymaar’s old feed, I didn’t think it needed another template. I thought it needed a reason for every piece of content to exist.</p></div></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-system"><span class="case-kicker">The content system</span><h2>Almost every worthwhile story a developer can tell comes back to three questions.</h2><div class="system-questions"><div><span>01</span><h3>Why are we doing it this way?</h3></div><div><span>02</span><h3>What are we actually building?</h3></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Who and what are we building around?</h3></div></div><p>Not three campaigns. Not three monthly themes. Three permanent lenses through which the company could see the world.</p></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-chapter"><div class="chapter-copy"><span>01 — Why This Way?</span><h2>A real-estate company with an opinion.</h2><p>I didn’t want Almaymaar to only participate in the real-estate conversation. I wanted it to question the assumptions of the industry it belonged to — from bad urban planning and disappearing courtyards to forgotten materials, patterns and ways of building.</p><p>A brand shouldn’t need to mention its product in every sentence to prove that it knows what it is talking about.</p></div><div class="triptych"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-why-3.png" alt="What Pakistan lost to bad urban planning"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-why-2.png" alt="Why does Pakistan always sink"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-why-1.png" alt="Why does Pakistani real-estate content scream sale"></div></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-chapter"><div class="chapter-copy"><span>02 — From the Site</span><h2>Progress became content.</h2><p>We build things. Yet real-estate marketing had become so obsessed with renders, launches and promises that the actual act of building had almost become background noise.</p><p>No pretending the building was finished. No hiding the concrete, steel, mud, cranes or scaffolding. The people, decisions and difficulty of building became part of the story.</p><blockquote>If you’re asking somebody to believe in something that doesn’t fully exist yet, the most powerful marketing isn’t another promise. It’s proof.</blockquote></div><figure class="almaymaar-wide"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-site-grid.jpg" alt="Almaymaar construction and site stories arranged in a three-column grid"></figure></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-grid-proof"><div class="almaymaar-section-head"><span>The design system</span><h2>Every column had a job.</h2></div><figure><img src="/assets/almaymaar-grid-system.jpg" alt="The three-column Almaymaar content system"></figure><div class="grid-legend"><div><span>Left</span><h3>Why This Way?</h3><p>Our point of view.</p></div><div><span>Centre</span><h3>From the Site</h3><p>Our proof.</p></div><div><span>Right</span><h3>People &amp; Places</h3><p>Our humanity.</p></div></div><p class="system-signoff">Think. Build. Belong.</p></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-chapter"><div class="chapter-copy"><span>03 — People &amp; Places</span><h2>Everything a building exists for.</h2><p>People. Streets. Craft. Memory. Culture. Cities. The things we inherit, the things we’re slowly losing, and the places that somehow stay with us.</p><p>People &amp; Places gave Almaymaar permission to look beyond its own boundary walls. Not because each subject could sell an apartment, but because all of them belonged to the larger conversation about how people inhabit places.</p><blockquote>Real estate is not property. It is people, and the places they call theirs.</blockquote></div><div class="triptych"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-people-1.png" alt="Patterns and their lost language"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-people-2.png" alt="Colors of Pakistan"><img src="/assets/almaymaar-people-3.png" alt="Doors of Pakistan"></div></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-shift"><div><span class="case-kicker">The internal shift</span><h2>The system changed more than the feed.</h2><p>Marketing stopped being treated only as the department that made posts, films and campaigns. People began involving it earlier. Ideas were discussed differently. Construction teams became part of storytelling. Culture became material.</p><p>The company started seeing marketing differently because it started seeing what marketing could be.</p></div><figure><img src="/assets/almaymaar-people-grid.jpg" alt="People, places and construction stories on the Almaymaar feed"></figure></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-result"><span class="case-kicker">The response</span><strong>1.5K → 8K+</strong><h2>Organic audience growth.</h2><p>Followers tell you that more people arrived. What matters is why they stayed. Almaymaar finally had something recognisable: different subjects connected by the same worldview.</p></section>
  <section class="almaymaar-closing"><div><p>Four years of real-estate marketing taught me something surprisingly simple.</p><h2>A developer really only has three stories to tell.</h2><div class="closing-lines"><span>Why it believes.</span><span>What it builds.</span><span>Who it builds for.</span></div><p>I just gave each one a place to live.</p></div><img src="/assets/almaymaar-closing-grid.jpg" alt="The evolved Almaymaar editorial feed"></section>
</article><a class="next almaymaar-next" href="/harsukh/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>The Harsukh ↗</span></a>`}
function harsukhCaseStudy(){return `<div class="almaymaar-opening"><img class="almaymaar-opening-image" src="/assets/harsukh-opening.png" alt="A mountain residence among snow-covered pine trees at dusk" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high"><div class="almaymaar-opening-caption"><span class="case-kicker">The Harsukh · Selected work</span><p>Head of Marketing · Creative &amp; Brand Lead<br>Brand Strategy · Creative Direction · Content Systems · Visual Identity · Storytelling</p></div></div>
<article class="harsukh-case">
  <section class="harsukh-copy harsukh-opening"><span class="case-kicker">The challenge</span><h2>A beautiful place without a world around it.</h2><p>Harsukh is a residential project in the mountains of Galiyat, ten minutes from Nathia Gali. It had natural beauty, but its communication was largely functional: property features, construction updates, investment explainers and isolated renders.</p><p>It told people what was being built, but rarely gave them a reason to feel something about it. My challenge was to change that by turning the journey from land to living into the story itself.</p></section>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The idea</span><h2>Before selling the future, we needed to build belief.</h2><p>The finished residences were still ahead of us. The construction site was happening now. Around it was something no render could manufacture: the landscape, weather, people and character of Galiyat.</p><p>Instead of choosing between aspiration and reality, I built the brand around both. We would show people where Harsukh was going, and exactly how it was getting there.</p></section>
  <section class="proof-section before-after"><div class="proof-label">Before</div><figure class="before-figure"><img src="/assets/harsukh-before.png" alt="Harsukh social feed before the new brand system"><figcaption>Communication built around individual posts, features and sales information.</figcaption></figure><div class="proof-label proof-label-after">After</div><figure class="after-figure"><img src="/assets/harsukh-after.jpg" alt="Warm, consistent Harsukh interior campaign grid"><figcaption>A warmer, atmospheric visual world connected to the landscape.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The visual language</span><h2>The grid stopped behaving like a catalogue. It started behaving like a brand.</h2><p>Architecture, interiors, typography, photography and environmental storytelling began speaking the same language. The first shift was consistency: every image belonged to one evolving world.</p></section>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The future</span><h2>We gave the future texture.</h2><p>Instead of using architectural renders as technical representations, we treated them as scenes from a life that could eventually happen here: quiet mornings, mountain views, warm interiors and bedrooms overlooking the forest.</p><p>The aspiration became less about square footage and more about what being there might feel like.</p></section>
  <figure class="case-media media-wide"><img src="/assets/harsukh-future-main.jpg" alt="Harsukh penthouse overlooking the mountains"><figcaption>The future — a life imagined inside the landscape.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="case-media media-contained"><img src="/assets/harsukh-future-pair.jpg" alt="Three bedroom sanctuary and signature two bedroom interiors"><figcaption>Three Bedroom Sanctuary · Signature Two Bedroom</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The present</span><h2>Then we showed what was physically being built.</h2><p>Construction became part of the brand: concrete pours, excavation, structure, weather, night shifts, machinery and progress. The unfinished building was evidence that the promise was becoming real.</p></section><section class="harsukh-film harsukh-film-inline" aria-label="Zenith — Harsukh flagship TVC"><button class="harsukh-video-cover" aria-label="Play Zenith — Harsukh flagship TVC"><img src="/assets/harsukh-zenith-thumbnail.jpg" alt="Zenith — Harsukh flagship TVC thumbnail"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span></button><p class="media-caption">Zenith — the flagship film that introduced the world of Harsukh.</p></section>
  <figure class="case-media media-wide"><img src="/assets/harsukh-construction-day.jpg" alt="Top-down view of construction at Harsukh"><figcaption>Just a vision, finding its form.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="case-media media-wide"><img src="/assets/harsukh-construction-night.jpg" alt="Harsukh construction continuing at night"><figcaption>The work continued after dark in the mountains of Galiyat.</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The people</span><h2>We put faces to the work.</h2><p>Behind every polished architectural visual were people building it in conditions most audiences would never see. We spoke to the labourers and let them talk about leaving home for work, the site and the reality of building in the mountains.</p><p>They were no longer background elements in construction footage. They became part of the Harsukh story.</p></section>
  <section class="people-proof"><figure><img src="/assets/harsukh-worker-red.jpg" alt="Harsukh construction worker wearing a red traditional cap"></figure><figure><img src="/assets/harsukh-worker-black.jpg" alt="Harsukh construction worker wearing a black headscarf"></figure><p>The people building Harsukh, Galiyat.</p></section>
  <section class="harsukh-copy"><span class="case-kicker">The place</span><h2>Galiyat became a recurring character.</h2><p>The forests, fog, seasons, roads and people surrounding Harsukh became part of the identity. Postcard from Galiyat, Letter to Pakistan and Land to Living helped us build a wider editorial world around the project.</p><p>Harsukh could talk about a mountain before it talked about an apartment.</p></section>
  <figure class="case-media media-contained"><img src="/assets/harsukh-place-grid.jpg" alt="Postcard from Galiyat, Land to Living and Above the Ordinary campaign grid"><figcaption>Postcard from Galiyat · Land to Living · Above the Ordinary</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="case-media media-wide"><img src="/assets/harsukh-letter.jpg" alt="Letter to Pakistan campaign showing Harsukh in the mountains"><figcaption>Letter to Pakistan — the place carried the brand.</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="system-section"><span class="case-kicker">One project · Three timelines</span><h2>Aspiration and transparency in the same brand.</h2><div class="timeline-grid"><div><span>01</span><h3>The Future</h3><p>What living at Harsukh could become.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>The Present</h3><p>What was physically being built today.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>People &amp; Place</h3><p>Who was building it, and the world surrounding it.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="proof-result"><div><span class="case-kicker">The response</span><h2>People saw the difference.</h2><p>Harsukh could sell without every piece of communication feeling like an advertisement. Construction became storytelling. Workers became protagonists. The landscape carried the brand.</p></div><div class="metric"><strong>8,862</strong><span>followers</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>632.1K</strong><span>views in days</span></div></section>
  <section class="harsukh-closing"><img src="/assets/harsukh-closing.jpg" alt="Atmospheric Galiyat landscape"><div><h2>We didn't hide the making of Harsukh.</h2><p>We made the making part of the brand.</p></div></section>
</article><a class="next" href="/downtownlahore/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>Downtown Lahore ↗</span></a>`}
function crafeCaseStudy(){return `<article class="crafe-case"><img class="crafe-hero" src="/assets/crafe-hero.png" alt="Crafé sign in warm afternoon light"><header class="crafe-title"><span>Crafé, Cantt Lahore</span><h1>Crafé Upstairs</h1><p>I turned an upstairs into somewhere people wanted to be.</p><small>Creative Director · Concept · Storytelling · Launch Campaign</small></header><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The brief</span><div><h2>A new floor needed a reason to exist.</h2><p>Crafé was already a familiar coffee shop in Cantt, Lahore. Then came Upstairs.</p><p>A new floor. An all-day breakfast and brunch space. Beautifully done, but still just a room above a coffee shop unless we could give people a reason to climb the stairs.</p></div></section><section class="crafe-super"><h2>I didn’t want to reveal it with a walkthrough.<br>I wanted to tell people why it was there.</h2></section><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The idea</span><div><h2>So I went back to the beginning.</h2><p>Before the menu, the furniture or the new space, there was the founder’s original thought behind Crafé. That became the story.</p><p>I built the reveal around that thought — where Crafé came from, what it wanted to feel like, and why Upstairs was a natural next chapter rather than simply an expansion.</p><p>The space only appeared once the audience understood the reason for it.</p></div></section><div class="crafe-grid"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0345.png" alt="A framed Crafé detail"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0339.jpg" alt="The opening story inside Crafé"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0342.png" alt="Wasib on the stairs leading upstairs"></div><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The reveal</span><div><h2>The reveal came last.</h2><p>We held the new space back. Then, gradually, the film moved upstairs.</p><p>Morning light. Breakfast on the table. Coffee. People settling in. The little details that make somewhere feel lived in.</p></div></section><section class="crafe-super"><h2>We weren’t revealing square footage.<br>We were revealing a new way to spend the morning at Crafé.</h2></section><div class="crafe-grid crafe-reveal"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0337.jpg" alt="People gathered in Crafé Upstairs"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0340.jpg" alt="Breakfast served at Crafé"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-img_0344.png" alt="Coffee beneath the skylight"></div><section class="crafe-watch"><div><h2>And people watched.</h2><p>What began as a reveal for a new floor became Crafé’s most-watched advertisement to date.</p><a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DI1AlO8hZ2y/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the original Instagram reel ↗</a></div><iframe loading="lazy" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/o6hx_V9Lxm8?rel=0" title="Crafé Upstairs launch film" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe></section><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The response</span><div><h2>It became Crafé Upstairs.</h2><p>More importantly, Upstairs stopped feeling like the new floor at Crafé. It became something people could name, remember and associate with its own experience.</p><p>The campaign helped put the space into people’s minds before many of them had even walked through the door.</p></div></section><figure class="crafe-campaign"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/crafe-campaign.png" alt="Crafé Upstairs campaign posts"><figcaption>The launch campaign.</figcaption></figure><section class="crafe-super"><h2>Sometimes creative direction isn’t about inventing a bigger idea.</h2><p>It’s about finding the idea that was already there — and telling it well enough that people finally notice it.</p></section></article><a class="next almaymaar-next" href="/kiapakistan/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>KIA Pakistan ↗</span></a>`}
function kiaCaseStudy(){return `<article class="crafe-case kia-case"><img class="kia-hero" src="/assets/kia/image1.png" alt="KIA Sorento in a mountain landscape"><header class="crafe-title"><span>KIA Pakistan</span><h1>A race without<br>a loser.</h1><p>I wrote a race where neither car could afford to lose.</p><small>Concept &amp; Ad Writing</small></header><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The brief</span><div><h2>Two SUVs. One journey.</h2><p>The all-new KIA Sportage and Sorento were ready to be introduced together. The starting point was simple: put them in a race.</p><p>Six of Pakistan’s leading creators. Two teams. Two SUVs. One journey. There was just one problem.</p></div></section><section class="crafe-super"><h2>Every race needs a loser.<br>A launch film couldn’t have one.</h2></section><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The idea</span><div><h2>Two different ways of getting to the same place.</h2><p>Sportage and Sorento weren’t competing to prove which was the better car. They represented two different ways of getting to the same place.</p><p>The competition gave us pace, personalities and unpredictability. The cars gave each team a different character.</p><p>So instead of writing a conventional automotive film around features and beauty shots, I developed a narrative where the product differences could emerge through the journey itself.</p></div></section><div class="kia-pair"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image7.png" alt="The journey begins in Islamabad"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image4.png" alt="Sportage and Sorento at the starting point"></div><section class="crafe-super"><h2>The race became the device.<br>The contrast became the story.</h2></section><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The cast</span><div><h2>Six personalities made it unpredictable.</h2><p>The film brought together Irfan Junejo, Laiba Khan Lodhi, Hirableeh, Ukhano, Mooroo and Rana Hamza Saif — creators with very different personalities and audiences.</p><p>That mattered. The concept needed enough structure to remain an advertisement, but enough freedom for six real personalities to make the journey feel spontaneous.</p><p>Instead of asking influencers to appear around the product, the idea put them inside the premise.</p></div></section><div class="kia-pair"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image6.png" alt="The creators discussing the race"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image8.png" alt="One team on the road"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image9.png" alt="The other team inside their SUV"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image12.png" alt="The six creators together"></div><section class="crafe-copy"><span>My contribution</span><div><h2>My job ended where production began.</h2><p>My role was the creative concept and ad writing. I developed the central race mechanic, the narrative logic behind putting the two vehicles against each other, and the creative problem the film had to solve:</p><p>How do you create competition between two products you’re launching simultaneously, without diminishing either one?</p><p>Once the concept was established, I handed it over to the agency, which developed the screenplay and handled production and execution.</p></div></section><figure class="kia-film"><button class="harsukh-video-cover" data-kia-play aria-label="Play KIA Pakistan launch film"><img src="/assets/kia/image3.png" alt="KIA Sportage launch film cover"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span></button><figcaption>Sportage vs Sorento — the full film.</figcaption></figure><section class="crafe-super"><h2>1.3 million views later.</h2><p>The film went on to generate 1.3M views on YouTube, bringing two major vehicle launches into one piece of entertainment without forcing either into second place.</p></section><figure class="kia-proof"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image2.png" alt="YouTube view count for the KIA launch film"><figcaption>YouTube performance, captured in the supplied screenshot.</figcaption></figure><figure class="kia-final"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/kia/image5.png" alt="Both SUVs at the journey’s destination"></figure><section class="crafe-copy"><span>The outcome</span><div><h2>We found a way to have the race without creating a loser.</h2><p>We didn’t remove the tension of the race. And that was ultimately the point.</p></div></section></article><a class="next almaymaar-next" href="/chakor/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>Chakor Ventures ↗</span></a>`}
document.addEventListener('click',event=>{const cover=event.target.closest('[data-kia-play]');if(cover)cover.outerHTML='<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/jI_Ist-3kj0?autoplay=1&rel=0" title="KIA Pakistan launch film" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>'});
function propertyFilm(id,title,short=false,thumb=''){return `<figure class="property-film ${short?'property-short':''}">${thumb?`<button class="property-video-cover" data-property-play="${id}" aria-label="Play ${title}"><img loading="lazy" src="${thumb}" alt="${title} thumbnail"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span></button>`:`<iframe loading="lazy" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/${id}?rel=0" title="${title}" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>`}<figcaption>${title}</figcaption></figure>`}
function propertyCopy(label,title,copy){return `<section class="crafe-copy"><span>${label}</span><div><h2>${title}</h2>${copy.map(t=>`<p>${t}</p>`).join('')}</div></section>`}
function propertyCaseStudy(slug){const chakor=slug==='chakor';return `<article class="crafe-case property-case ${chakor?'chakor-case':'imarat-case'}">${chakor?'<figure class="property-hero"><img src="/assets/chakor-hero.png" alt="Chakor Ventures construction site and city skyline"></figure>':'<figure class="property-hero"><img src="/assets/imarat-hero.png" alt="IMARAT residence overlooking a mountain lake at sunset"></figure>'}<header class="crafe-title"><span>${chakor?'Chakor Ventures · 2023–2024':'IMARAT / Graana.com · 2020–2023'}</span><h1>${chakor?'Make the offer<br>make sense.':'Make the scale<br>understandable.'}</h1><p>${chakor?'I turned a payment structure into something people could follow.':'I helped people see the idea behind the development.'}</p><small>${chakor?'Creative Strategist':'Creative &amp; Brand Manager'} · Concept · Messaging · On-camera Presentation</small></header>${chakor?`
${propertyCopy('Citadel 7','A clear offer needed a clear story.',['Chakor Ventures develops commercial and residential projects in Pakistan. At Citadel 7, the challenge was to explain the project’s location, commercial potential and payment offer in a way prospective buyers could understand.','I contributed to campaign concepts, messaging and digital content, and presented the explainers on camera.'])}
<section class="crafe-super"><h2>60% upfront.<br>40% at completion.</h2><p>The campaign’s 60–40 structure was simple. The work was making it clear, memorable and easy to discuss.</p></section>
${propertyCopy('The campaign explainer','I became both sides of the conversation.',['I contributed to the concept and messaging for an interview-style format, appearing as both host and guest. One version of me asked the questions; the other unpacked the offer.','The conversational setup gave the film a visual hook while helping prospective buyers understand what they would pay upfront and what remained payable at completion and handover.'])}
${propertyFilm('faQtSpEsjEs','Citadel 7 — the 60–40 campaign explainer',false,'/assets/chakor-citadel-thumbnail.png')}
${propertyCopy('On location','Put the project in context.',['The next explainer took the story onto the development site. I contributed to its messaging and structure and presented the project’s location advantages, architectural concept and commercial potential.','Being on site helped audiences connect the explanation to the physical scale of Citadel 7.'])}
${propertyFilm('LVf2fVPvxJs','Citadel 7 — on-site project explainer')}
<section class="crafe-super"><h2>The location became<br>the visual hook.</h2></section>
${propertyCopy('A different perspective','Show the surroundings. Explain the opportunity.',['A further film used a high-elevation viewpoint from the site to show the surrounding area and connectivity. I contributed to the campaign messaging and presented the location story alongside the 60–40 offer.','The vantage point captured attention while giving the explanation a visible reference.'])}
${propertyFilm('uYd2zh-l6YQ','Citadel 7 — location and 60–40 offer',true)}
${propertyCopy('The contribution','Content the sales team could use.',['The explainers ran across digital channels and supported client discussions. They helped communicate the payment structure, physical context and commercial proposition, contributing to interest and inquiries.','The aim was consistent across every format: give people a clearer understanding of what they were being asked to consider.'])}
`: `${propertyCopy('The starting point','Large projects. A human explanation.',['IMARAT / Graana.com operates across real estate development, technology and brokerage in Pakistan. As Creative & Brand Manager, I developed and executed digital marketing content aligned with brand positioning and audience engagement.','The explainers connected project ideas to information prospective investors could understand and sales teams could use.'])}
<section class="crafe-super"><h2>Start with a story<br>people already know.</h2></section>
<figure class="property-theme"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/imarat-grand-bazaar.png" alt="IMARAT Grand Bazaar presentation above Lahore"></figure>${propertyCopy('Grand Bazaar','From Raja Bazaar to a modern marketplace.',['Grand Bazaar was introduced through the historic trading culture of Raja Bazaar. The story connected the legacy of traditional commerce with a contemporary retail destination on the main Islamabad Expressway.','I contributed to the concept and messaging and served as the on-camera presenter, communicating the vision, strategic location and commercial potential behind the development.'])}
${propertyFilm('okMpCKULTUE','Grand Bazaar — concept introduction')}
${propertyCopy('The purpose','Turn the concept into a conversation.',['The video helped potential investors understand the project’s idea and commercial opportunity. It was shared across digital channels and used by the sales team in client presentations, supporting investor interest and commercial-unit sales.'])}
<section class="crafe-super"><h2>Scale only matters<br>when people can understand it.</h2></section>
${propertyCopy('Mall of IMARAT','Make a major retail development understandable.',['The Mall of IMARAT explainer introduced its location, architectural scale and commercial value proposition, including a leasable area exceeding one million square feet.','I contributed to the explainer content and presented it on camera, translating the project’s features into an overview intended for prospective investors and buyers.'])}
${propertyFilm('7y_tU4MMcJg','Mall of IMARAT — project explainer',false,'/assets/imarat-mall-thumbnail.png')}
${propertyCopy('The contribution','A useful story beyond the screen.',['The film gave the sales team a clear overview to share during meetings and presentations. It helped audiences visualise the development’s scale and positioning and supported inquiries and leads.','These projects brought together brand storytelling, investor communication and on-camera presentation: finding the idea inside a large development and making it easier to understand.'])}
`}</article><a class="next almaymaar-next" href="/${chakor?'imarat':'work'}/" data-link><span>${chakor?'Next project':'Back to'}</span><span>${chakor?'IMARAT':'Portfolio'} ↗</span></a>`}
function flapWord(word){return `<span class="flap-word">${[...word].map(letter=>`<i>${letter}</i>`).join('')}</span>`}
function downtownCaseStudy(){return `<section class="downtown-board" aria-label="Downtown Lahore split-flap destination board"><div class="board-meta"><span>Gate 42B <b></b> Boarding</span><span>Est. departure: 23:45</span></div><div class="flap-line">${flapWord('DOWNTOWN')}</div><div class="flap-line flap-line-second">${flapWord('LAHORE')}</div><div class="board-rule"></div><p>A new destination is arriving.</p></section><section class="downtown-title"><span class="case-kicker">Selected work · Film &amp; destination storytelling</span><h1>Downtown<br>Lahore</h1><p>I sell a place by selling the idea of it.</p></section><article class="dt-case"><section class="dt-copy"><span>Vision Group × ParkView City Lahore</span><div><h2>How do you reveal a place that isn’t there yet?</h2><p>Downtown Lahore hadn&#x27;t been built.</p><p>There was no finished place to walk through. No streets, no storefronts, no life inside it to capture. But we still had to introduce it in a way that made people understand what it could become.</p><p>That was the brief I found interesting.</p><p>Instead of pretending the future was already here, I built the film around the idea of it.</p></div></section><div class="dt-images"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-1.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-2.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"></div><section class="dt-super"><h2>The place wasn’t there.<br>The story had to be.</h2></section><section class="dt-copy"><span>The approach</span><div><h2>So I started with what we actually had.</h2><p>The city around it. The site. The ambition behind the project. And a camera.</p><p>I wanted the film to feel closer to something you would stop and watch than something you immediately recognised as a real-estate advertisement.</p><p>Less announcing. More storytelling.</p><p>I developed the concept, wrote the script and directed the film. And because the storytelling depended on someone taking the audience through that idea, I stepped in front of the camera and performed it too.</p></div></section><div class="dt-images"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-3.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-5.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-6.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-7.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"></div><section class="dt-process">Concept → Writing → Direction → Performance</section><section class="dt-copy"><span>The writing</span><div><h2>The writing had one rule.</h2><p>Don&#x27;t tell what you can show.</p><p>Don&#x27;t show what you can tell.</p><p>That thinking shaped the script, the locations and eventually the edit.</p><p>The film didn&#x27;t need to explain every feature of Downtown Lahore. It needed to leave you with a feeling for the kind of place it wanted to become.</p><p>For me, that was the difference between advertising a development and telling the story of one.</p></div></section><figure class="dt-film"><button class="harsukh-video-cover dt-video-cover" aria-label="Play Downtown Lahore film"><img src="/assets/downtown-video-cover.png" alt="Wasib presenting Downtown Lahore in front of Badshahi Mosque"><span aria-hidden="true">▶</span></button><figcaption>Downtown Lahore — the complete film</figcaption></figure><section class="dt-super"><h2>A city. A future.<br>A downtown yet to come.</h2></section><section class="dt-copy"><span>Beyond the feed</span><div><h2>Then it went somewhere we hadn’t made it for.</h2><p>The film was created for social media.</p><p>Then Samaa TV aired it on national television.</p></div></section><figure class="dt-broadcast"><img src="/assets/downtown-samaa.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film broadcast on Samaa TV"><figcaption>The film on Samaa TV.</figcaption></figure><section class="dt-super"><h2>From Instagram<br>to national television.</h2></section><section class="dt-copy"><span>What it meant</span><div><h2>Digital storytelling could command the same space.</h2><p>The normal journey was the other way around: make the television commercial first, then cut it down for digital.</p><p>This was a social-first film appearing in a mainstream broadcast environment alongside conventional advertising.</p><p>It reinforced something I was already beginning to believe:</p><p>Digital storytelling didn&#x27;t need to imitate traditional advertising to command the same space.</p></div></section><div class="dt-images"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-8.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-10.png" alt="Downtown Lahore film still"></div><figure class="dt-finale"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/downtown-still-13.png" alt="Downtown Lahore fountains at night"></figure><section class="dt-copy"><span>The lesson</span><div><h2>Market the idea of a place before the place itself exists.</h2><p>Downtown Lahore taught me that. And that lesson stayed with me long after the film.</p><p>Vision Group × ParkView City Lahore</p><p>Creative Lead · Concept · Writing · Direction · Performance</p></div></section></article><a class="next downtown-next" href="/crafeupstairs/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>Crafé Upstairs ↗</span></a>`}
function project(p){if(p.slug==='chakor'||p.slug==='imarat')return propertyCaseStudy(p.slug);if(p.slug==='kiapakistan')return kiaCaseStudy();if(p.slug==='crafeupstairs')return crafeCaseStudy();if(p.slug==='almaymaar')return almaymaarCaseStudy();if(p.slug==='harsukh')return harsukhCaseStudy();if(p.slug==='downtownlahore')return downtownCaseStudy();const next=projects[(projects.indexOf(p)+1)%projects.length];return `<section class="project-hero"><div class="project-title"><span class="eyebrow">Selected work</span><h1>${p.name}</h1><p>${p.line}</p></div>${p.image?`<div class="project-image"><img src="${p.image}" alt="${esc(p.name)} project image"></div>`:`<div class="project-image placeholder">${p.name}</div>`}</section><article class="case-body">${p.blocks.map(b=>`<section class="case-block"><h2>${b[0]}</h2><p>${b[1]}</p></section>`).join('')}${p.gallery?`<div class="gallery">${p.gallery.map((im,i)=>`<img src="${im}" alt="${esc(p.name)} project detail ${i+1}">`).join('')}</div>`:''}</article><a class="next" href="/${next.slug}/" data-link><span>Next project</span><span>${next.name} ↗</span></a>`}
function about(){return `<section class="about-grid"><div class="about-image"><img src="/assets/about.png" alt="Portrait of Wasib Imdad"></div><article class="about-copy"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>I just want to <em>make things.</em></h1><p>Hi, I’m Wasib. I’m a Creative Director, but I’ve never been particularly interested in staying inside the boundaries of a job title.</p><p>I like ideas. More specifically, I like what happens when an idea leaves someone’s head and becomes something real.</p><p>A brand people recognise. A film people remember. A place people want to visit. A product people want to hold. A story that makes something ordinary feel worth paying attention to.</p><p>I enjoy the making as much as the thinking. I want to shape the frame, question the type, change the edit, rewrite the line, move the image and keep going until the thing feels right.</p><p class="question">How do we make someone care?</p><p>Sometimes the answer is a brand. Sometimes it’s a campaign. Sometimes it’s a thirty-second film. Sometimes it’s just one sentence in exactly the right place.</p><p>I don’t think good creative work needs to shout to be powerful. It just needs to make you stop for a second.</p><p>That’s what I’m trying to make. Things that are useful, thoughtful and carefully made. Things with a point of view. Things people can feel.</p></article></section>`}
function contact(){return `<section class="contact-page"><span class="eyebrow">Have a project in mind?</span><div><h1>Let’s make<br>something<br>worth feeling.</h1><a class="email" href="mailto:wasib@wasib.co">wasib@wasib.co ↗</a><div class="contact-links"><a href="https://instagram.com/wasib25">Instagram</a><a href="https://linkedin.com">LinkedIn</a></div></div></section>`}
function render(){const path=location.pathname.replace(/^\/+|\/+$/g,'');let html;if(!path)html=home();else if(path==='work')html=work();else if(path==='about')html=about();else if(path==='contact')html=contact();else{const p=projects.find(x=>x.slug===path);html=p?project(p):work()}document.body.classList.toggle('is-work-page',path==='work');app.innerHTML=html;document.querySelectorAll('[data-property-play]').forEach(cover=>cover.onclick=()=>{const id=cover.dataset.propertyPlay;cover.parentElement.innerHTML=`<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1&rel=0" title="Property explainer" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>`});const dtCover=app.querySelector('.dt-video-cover');if(dtCover)dtCover.onclick=()=>{dtCover.outerHTML='<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/gCq7XP2yFVA?autoplay=1&rel=0" title="Downtown Lahore film" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>'};const filmCover=app.querySelector('.harsukh-film .harsukh-video-cover');if(filmCover)filmCover.onclick=()=>{filmCover.parentElement.innerHTML='<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/esNzIPFY9hE?autoplay=1&rel=0" title="Zenith — Harsukh flagship TVC" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>'};document.title=path?`${path==='work'?'Work':path==='about'?'About':path==='contact'?'Contact':projects.find(x=>x.slug===path)?.name||'Work'} — Wasib Imdad`:'Wasib Imdad — Creative Director';document.querySelectorAll('[data-link]').forEach(a=>a.onclick=e=>{e.preventDefault();history.pushState({},'',a.href);render();scrollTo(0,0)});document.querySelector('#year').textContent=new Date().getFullYear()}
document.querySelector('.menu').onclick=e=>{const n=document.querySelector('.site-header nav');n.classList.toggle('open');e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-expanded',n.classList.contains('open'));e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-label',n.classList.contains('open')?'Close menu':'Open menu')};document.querySelectorAll('.site-header nav a').forEach(a=>a.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelector('.site-header nav').classList.remove('open');const menu=document.querySelector('.menu');menu.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');menu.setAttribute('aria-label','Open menu')}));addEventListener('popstate',render);render();
